title: "L0-b  States of the budget bill, from proposal to law"
---
stateDiagram-v2
  direction TB
  %% QUESTION THIS DIAGRAM ANSWERS: in which state is the budget of a fiscal year at a given date, and which act moves it to the next state?
  %% READING: one box = one state of the document. The text on an arrow = the act and the body that performs it.
  %% SOURCES: [CONST VII.22] submission. [CONST VI.24] the bill starts in the House. [CONST VI.25(7)] reenactment. [CONST VI.27(2)] item veto. [INQ-GUIDE] the stages in Congress and the two-thirds override. [NBC599] the dates of the FY 2026 example.
  %% GENERAL KNOWLEDGE, NOT OPENED IN A SOURCE HERE: the names of the readings and the publication step.

  state "Proposed by the President (NEP, BESF, Budget Message)" as NEP
  state "General Appropriations Bill in the House committee" as HCOM
  state "Approved by the House on third reading" as HAPP
  state "Approved by the Senate with amendments" as SAPP
  state "In the bicameral conference committee" as BICAM
  state "Conference report ratified by both chambers" as RATIF
  state "Enrolled bill with the President" as ENR
  state "General Appropriations Act (GAA) in effect" as GAA
  state "Item vetoed" as VETO
  state "Previous GAA deemed re-enacted" as REEN

  [*] --> NEP: President submits within 30 days from the opening of the regular session
  NEP --> HCOM: filed in the House and referred to the Committee on Appropriations
  HCOM --> HAPP: committee report, plenary debates, amendments, vote
  HAPP --> SAPP: Senate committee and plenary act on the House bill
  SAPP --> BICAM: the two versions differ
  BICAM --> RATIF: conferees agree, both chambers ratify
  RATIF --> ENR: sent to the President
  ENR --> GAA: President signs
  ENR --> VETO: President vetoes particular items
  VETO --> GAA: Congress overrides by two thirds of each chamber
  VETO --> [*]: the item is not law
  NEP --> REEN: the fiscal year starts and no GAA is in force
  REEN --> GAA: the new GAA takes effect (FY 2026 example, 5 January 2026)
  GAA --> [*]: execution starts (chapter E0)
